<!--TITLE: FAQ | APU CodeStorm 2026-->
<!--DESC: Frequently asked questions about APU CodeStorm 2026 - eligibility, registration, judging, welfare and logistics.-->
<section class="page-header" style="background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(11,18,32,.82),rgba(11,18,32,.92)),url('assets/img/faq-banner.svg')">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="index.html">Home</a> &rsaquo; FAQ</p>
    <span class="kicker">Answers</span>
    <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="lead">If your question is not here, the committee replies to the contact form within two
      working days.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="kicker">General</span>
      <h2>About the event</h2>
    </div>

    <details class="accordion" open>
      <summary class="accordion__btn">What is APU CodeStorm 2026?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>It is a fictional 48-hour interfaculty hackathon created for the
        CT053-3-1 web design assignment. In the world of this site, teams of three to four students
        build working prototypes across six challenge tracks, mentored by industry engineers and
        judged on demo day.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Who can take part?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Any student currently enrolled at APU, from any faculty and any
        intake. Teams need three or four members, and at least one member must be in their first or
        second year. Solo participants can join the team-formation mixer on Friday morning.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Does it cost anything?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>No. Registration, meals, merch and workshop materials are covered
        by the sponsor pool. Teams only cover their own transport if they are commuting from outside
        Cyberjaya.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Do I need to be a programmer?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>No. Strong teams mix developers with designers, writers, business
        students and domain experts. The UI Design Sprint and Lightning Talk Battle are also open to
        students who do not write code at all.</p></div>
    </details>

    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <span class="kicker">Registration</span>
      <h2>Signing up</h2>
    </div>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">How do I register my team?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Fill in the registration form once, with the captain as the
        submitter. Add the other members in section 3. You will receive a team code by e-mail within
        two working days, and you can edit your roster from the participant dashboard until 27 November.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Can I change teams after registering?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Yes, once. Send the request through the contact form before
        9 March and the committee will move you. After confirmations go out, rosters are locked so
        judging sheets stay accurate.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">What if my team is missing a member?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Register anyway. Unfilled seats are matched during the formation
        mixer at 10:30 on Friday, where solo participants pitch themselves to teams that need help.</p></div>
    </details>

    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <span class="kicker">During the event</span>
      <h2>The 48 hours</h2>
    </div>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Do we have to stay overnight?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>No. The build floor is open around the clock, but overnight stays
        are optional and the campus closes the atrium between 01:00 and 06:00. Welfare staff are on
        call throughout, and a quiet room is available 24 hours.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">What can we use from outside sources?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Open-source libraries, public APIs, pre-trained models, stock
        media and starter templates are allowed when credited in the build log. Code written before the
        kickoff must be declared; undeclared outside code counts as plagiarism.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">What do we submit?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>A repository link, the build log, a slide deck and a demo video
        under 200 MB, all uploaded through the participant dashboard before the code freeze at 12:00 on
        Sunday 6 December.</p></div>
    </details>

    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <span class="kicker">Judging &amp; prizes</span>
      <h2>Scoring</h2>
    </div>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">How is the winner decided?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Each track is scored on the published rubric - innovation, technical
        execution, user experience, impact and pitch quality - by a panel of two academics and one
        industry judge. The Grand Champion is the highest-scoring track winner, and ties are broken by
        the People's Choice vote.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">What are the prizes?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>A RM 20,000 pool split across six track winners, plus the Grand
        Champion, People's Choice and the UI Design Sprint. Prizes include cash vouchers, internship
        interviews with partner companies and one year of developer tooling credits.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Will we get feedback if we lose?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Yes. Every team receives the judges' written score sheets by e-mail
        within five working days, including the marks lost on each rubric line.</p></div>
    </details>

    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <span class="kicker">Logistics</span>
      <h2>Venue, food and welfare</h2>
    </div>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Where is the event held?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Block C of the APU Cyberjaya campus - Lecture Theatre 1 for keynotes
        and judging, the Level 3 Innovation Lab for building, and the Level 1 cafeteria for meals. See
        the <a href="contact.html#map">venue map</a>.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">Is food provided?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Three meals, two coffee breaks and a midnight snack each day.
        Dietary requirements are collected on the registration form, and halal and vegetarian options
        are always available.</p></div>
    </details>

    <details class="accordion">
      <summary class="accordion__btn">How do I report a problem?</summary>
      <div class="accordion__body"><p>Use the contact form, find the welfare desk in the Innovation Lab,
        or e-mail codestorm@apu.edu.my. Reports are confidential and answered within 24 hours during the
        event.</p></div>
    </details>

    <div class="alert alert--ok" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <p><strong>Still stuck?</strong> Send the committee a message and we will answer within two
        working days.</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="contact.html">Ask a question</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
